; Three shapes whose boundaries curve, none of which is written as segments.
;
; Every arc here is a centre and a point on the wall claimed on the edge itself, so the
; curve stays a curve for as long as the model does. What its sag comes to is
; computed from the circle each time it is asked and is never baked in at
; whatever resolution somebody happened to be drawing at.

; A room whose east wall bows out into a semicircular bay.
(vertex geom:V-01
  (label "Bay room, corner 1")
  (frame frame:building)
  (position
    (value (0.0 0.0 0.0) m)
    (source "Interior control set IC-01, Acme Surveys")
    (method method:total-station)
    (accuracy (independent 0.004 m) (systematic 0.008 m control:CP-3))
    (date "2026-02-18")))
(vertex geom:V-02
  (label "Bay room, corner 2")
